      "filePath": ".agents/guides/connect-state.md",
      "summary": "Architecture guide for the Spotify Connect subsystem — covering DealerClient WebSocket, DeviceStateManager PutState announce, PlaybackStateManager cluster state, ConnectCommandClient remote commands, and all related UI surfaces (device picker, now-playing, volume, connect-debug).",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "spotify-connect", "networking"],
      "complexity": "complex"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:.agents/guides/content-card.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "content-card.md",
      "filePath": ".agents/guides/content-card.md",
      "summary": "Architecture guide for the ContentCard reusable shelf/grid card control — covering its four partial-class structure, all XAML consumers across Home/Search/Browse/Library/Artist/Album/Show/Concert/Profile/Local pages, lifecycle viewport gating, attached behaviors, and image loading pipeline.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "ui-component", "component"],
      "complexity": "complex"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:.agents/guides/discography-expander.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "discography-expander.md",
      "filePath": ".agents/guides/discography-expander.md",
      "summary": "Architecture guide for the artist-page inline album expander — documenting ExpandableAlbumGrid, the custom ExpandingGridLayout virtualizing layout with reserved band, and the AlbumDetailPanel overlay, including its expand/collapse data flow and the pitfalls of earlier abandoned approaches.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "ui-component", "discography"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:.agents/guides/library-and-sync.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "library-and-sync.md",
      "filePath": ".agents/guides/library-and-sync.md",
      "summary": "Architecture guide for the user-library lifecycle — collection sync (Liked Songs, Saved Albums, Artists, Shows, Pins, Listen Later, Bans), SQLite persistence via IMetadataDatabase, dealer-driven incremental updates, save/pin/follow write paths, and every library and playlist UI surface.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "library", "sync"],
      "complexity": "complex"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:.agents/guides/playback.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "playback.md",
      "filePath": ".agents/guides/playback.md",
      "summary": "Architecture guide for the local playback runtime spanning two processes — orchestrator, queue+context, track resolution, AudioHost IPC contract, decode/decrypt/DSP/EQ pipeline, prefetch, crossfade, local-file playback, video playback, SMTC integration, and the UI-side playback service.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "playback", "audio"],
      "complexity": "complex"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:.agents/guides/queue.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "queue.md",
      "filePath": ".agents/guides/queue.md",
      "summary": "Deep-dive architecture guide for the playback queue subsystem — the three-bucket in-memory model (user queue, context, post-context), cursor/shuffle/repeat semantics, pagination signals, autoplay rollover, cluster sync (PutState prev/next + QueueRevision), the QueueControl UI, drag-drop, and SetQueue/AddToQueue dealer commands.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "queue", "playback"],
      "complexity": "complex"
    },
    {
      "id": "document:.agents/guides/track-and-episode-ui.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "track-and-episode-ui.md",
